c_test/common: 
	inclues common ctest infra-structure source, like 
ctest engine core, ctest-sequencer which invokes each
testcases as per selected test-ip and test configuration.

c_test/logs: contains the ctest testcases logs.

c_test/hal:
	The platform/hardware abstraction layer (hal) 
includes hardware dependent source code, APIs like
io read/write, interrupt helper APIs, etc.
supported platform includes 
	arc : arc processor based board
	vcs : vcs simulator platform
	csim : c-based sw simulation
	pc : pc based platform.

c_test/config:
	includes various ctest configuration for supported IPs.

c_test/build:
	Includes all build related output files.

c_test/drv:
	Includes drivers for supported IPs like
mshc (mass storage host controller), msdc (mass storage 
device controller), i3c, network drivers for cgmac etc.

c_test/main:
	Includes the main application entry for each supported IPs.

ctest/os:
	support ctask schedular, which is os(linux) or non-os based,
supporting basic task managment API's and synchronization locks
like semaphores.

c_test/test:
	includes the ctest test routines for supported IPs

c_test/tools:
	includes optional tools like interactive terminal console
based on UART, where user can invoke the independent test-case from
terminal, read/write to device registers, memory dump for debug
purpose during development.

3.C_TEST configuration
====================
	The C_Test configuration for selected IP based set of
key value pairs data.
	Syntax: <key>=<value>

3.1 MSHC configuration
======================
	The Mass storage host controller configuration (mshc) options
includes
Datawidth = <1/4/8> 
	- 1 bit mode
	- 4 bit mode
	- 8 bit mode
speed-mode = SDR50, SDR104, HS200, HS400
data-transfer = PIO/SDMA/ADMA2/ADMA3
CQE - command queueing engine = <"enabled", "disabled">

4.0 CTest Automation and Test logs.
===================================
	- details on jenkins build automation
and test infrasturcre 

5.0 Build procedure
===================
	The top level CTest directory includes Makefile, which compiles and
builds the MHSC CTest application using the configuration file for MSHC driver
is available in config directory.
	Config/config.h –  Top level CTest configuration file
	Config/mshc_config.h -  MSHC driver configuration
GNU tool chain version 4.8.5 used for build CTest.

1)	Change to C_Test directory
	a.	# cd c_tests
	4.	Make clean
2)	# Make clean
3)	Building MHSC CTest
	#make

Make build MSHC CTest, the application build/mshc_main is created.

Note: The MSHC-CTest uses libpci-dev (option -lpci used), make
sure you install libpci-dev.

- refer to MSHC-CTEST User Guide for more information

